## Attached maps (owner principle 13; owner feedback Oct 15 2026)

Owner: "The Decades floor plan is wonderful." / "the Lima Twist one can be separated into four areas.. this will help smaller screens; also the DJ Booth is 106. Make DJ Booth color Blue, consistent throughout the floor plans. Denote Green for available and Red for booked tables. For floor maps ensure they are viewable from the phone."

- Decades (1024×619): 11 bookable, 3 areas — `decades-north-vip` "North VIP" (printed VIP TABLES: C1–C5), `decades-floor` "Floor" (polygon: C6–C9 + DJ BOOTH), `decades-south-vip` "South VIP" (printed VIP TABLES: C10–C11). Non-bookable BAR, DJ BOOTH, Emergency Exit, stairs, 1 unlabeled enclosure.
- Lima Twist Club, Washington DC (1024×382): **27 bookable** (24 tables + rounds 501–503); **106 = DJ BOOTH** (`{label:"106", name:"DJ BOOTH", type:"djBooth", bookable:false}` — printed label kept); **BAR1 / BAR2 not bookable** (grey). 4 areas (names club-editable): A "Area A · 200 Row" (201–209), B "Area B · DJ & 100 Row" (101–105 + 106), C "Area C · Bar & 400s" (401–403 + bars), D "Area D · 300s & Rounds" (301–307, 501–503). Owner: the image is the complete plan (no walls / exits drawn).
- **Bars are never bookable** (owner Oct 15 2026) — Decades BAR and Lima Twist BAR1 / BAR2 sit in `nonBookable[]`, along with DJ booths, exits, stairs, restrooms, stages.
- **Capacity:** each section has `maxCapacity` (max guests), `includedGuests` (covered by the minimum, 1..max), `minimumAmount`, optional `extraGuestFee` (VIP entry per guest beyond `includedGuests`; null when included = max), `deposit`. Booking stores `partySize ≤ maxCapacity`, `extraGuests = max(0, partySize − includedGuests)`, `extraGuestFeeTotal` computed server-side; Stripe Checkout gets a separate "Extra guests — VIP entry" line with `quantity: extraGuests`. Club Admin section editor exposes all five fields; per-night overrides never raise `maxCapacity`. Placeholder totals: Decades 80 max / 58 included; Lima Twist 90 / 80.
- **Ingest workflow** (always-on procedure `vip-floorplan-ingest.mdc`): uploaded → processing (Master Admin) → review (club admin confirms names / capacities / prices) → approved → published (Master Admin load, reason + chained audit `vip.floorplan_*`); rejected from any state. Clubs cannot use a plan until it is published. Master Admin help topic `help-vip-floorplan-ingest` (draft in proposal §15; register only when built).
- Photos: `reports/vip-floorplans/photo-match.md` — each club has one cover photo + logo, no gallery, 0 `clubMedia` rows; no photo matches a table with useful confidence.
- Schema `floqr.vipFloorPlan/2`: `areas[] {id, label (printed or null), name (club-editable), shape + rect|polygon, bounds, viewBox (phone zoom target), sectionIds, nonBookableIds}`; every bookable section in exactly one area; non-bookable items carry `type`, `state` (`djBooth` | `notBookable`), `areaId?`.
- Capacities / amounts are placeholders. Regenerate with `node reports/vip-floorplans/build-plans.js reports/vip-floorplans`; screenshots `node reports/vip-floorplans/shoot.mjs`.

## Shared color legend (one spec: `reports/vip-floorplans/legend.json`)

| State | Color | Icon | Pattern |
|---|---|---|---|
| Available | green `#22c55e` / stroke `#4ade80` | check | solid |
| Held | amber `#f59e0b` / `#fbbf24` | clock | diagonal stripes |
| Booked | red `#ef4444` / `#f87171` | cross | cross-hatch |
| Not bookable | grey `#9ca3af` dashed | lock | dots |
| DJ booth (every plan) | blue `#3b82f6` / `#60a5fa` | music | solid |
| Selected | yellow `#fde047` 4px ring, pulse (off under reduced motion) | — | — |

- **Use everywhere:** map, list, area chips, door view, 360 hotspots and embed. Clubs cannot recolor states; they can only rename areas.
- **Not color alone (WCAG 1.4.1):** every state also has an icon, a pattern and text, plus an on-map legend.
- **Contrast (1.4.11):** strokes are ≥ 3:1 on the map backgrounds. The build fails below that.

## Phone-first viewer

| Width | Behavior |
|---|---|
| ≤ 600px | Opens on the first area. Area chips with free counts. Zoom so the narrowest bookable section is ≥ 44px; hit rects padded to 44×44. Pinch and pan. Minimap + zoom buttons sit **under** the map, never over tables. The Overview shows one 44px badge per area, and table details open in a bottom sheet. |
| Tablet / PC | Full map with dashed area outlines; targets ≥ 24px; side or below details. |

There is always an accessible list grouped by area. Demo files: `preview.html`, `viewer.js`, `viewer.css`. QA uses `shoot.mjs`, which runs CDP device emulation. Do not use `--window-size` screenshots: headless enforces a ~500px minimum width, so a 390px shot is really a crop of a wider layout. Each shot reports the smallest target and the horizontal overflow.

## 3D / interactive ("Explore the room")

- **Must:** the 2D floor plan stays the booking UI.
- **Should:** an optional 360° panorama (Pannellum / Marzipano / Photo Sphere Viewer).
  - Hotspots `{sectionId, yaw, pitch}` in `vipPanoramas`.
  - A hotspot opens the same `select(sectionId)` → `createVipHold`, never a second booking path.
  - Lazy-loaded; first view ≤ 1.5 MB.
  - Capture is one position per area, with the venue closed and faces blurred.
  - The master image is CC (private) and deleted 30 days after replacement; published tiles are P.
  - Publish goes through `FLOQRReasonPrompt` and a chained audit row.
- **Could:** stylized three.js extrusion (needs walls), Gaussian splats (dark rooms reconstruct poorly), and a Matterport link-out only when a venue already has a tour.
- Full comparison, capture guide and budgets: proposal §13.6.

